<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea June agricultural import prices down - AFTAK.</title>
<headline>S.Korea June agricultural import prices down - AFTAK.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's agricultural commodities import prices fell in June from the previous month on declining prices in world markets, the Association of Foreign Trading Agents of Korea (AFTAK) said on Friday.</p>
<p>AFTAK, established in 1970, currently has 13,200 members representing more than 45,000 overseas suppliers.</p>
<p>Its member firms handle over 82 percent of the country's total agricultural imports.</p>
<p>June import prices for agricultural commodities were as follows:</p>
<p>(US$ per tonne on C&amp;F)  </p>
<p> COMMODITY   TYPE			 ORIGIN     Jun    May</p>
<p> Wheat	 Soft White		 U.S.	 166    196</p>
<p> Wheat	 Hard Red Winter	  U.S.	 173    202</p>
<p> Wheat	 Dark Northern Spring   U.S.	 197    207</p>
<p> Corn	  No.3 yellow		U.S.	 126    138</p>
<p> Soybean     No.2			 U.S.	 330    342</p>
<p> Soymeal				    U.S.	 280    320</p>
<p> Tallow	TW (FOB)		   U.S.	 455    460</p>
<p> Palm oil    Olein (FOB)		Malaysia   555    575</p>
<p> Sugar	 96-97 pct		  Tailand    300    295</p>
<p> Coffee	NY No.2 (FOB)	    Brazil   4,241  4,994</p>
<p> Rubber	RSS No.3		   Malaysia 1,067  1,147</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651 ENSA</p>
